  "why": "Two repositories writing one physical table. Without the join each gets its own `invoices` entity, so \"who writes this table\" answers per repository and silently under-reports \u2014 a schema change looks safe because half its writers are in a graph nobody merged. The declaration names billing as the schema owner; reporting's node collapses onto it. `ledger` is the control: reporting owns it, billing has never heard of it, and it must survive untouched \u2014 a joiner that collapsed every entity would pass on invoices and destroy this.",
